# 24. STRICT IMPLEMENTATION RULES

Follow these rules throughout the project.

1. Inspect before modifying.
2. Preserve existing working features.
3. Never rebuild the entire application unnecessarily.
4. Do not delete existing database records.
5. Never use destructive database migrations.
6. Never hardcode production API credentials.
7. Do not put AI logic directly inside UI components.
8. Avoid duplicate services and repositories.
9. Use reusable components and centralized configuration.
10. Keep processing operations recoverable.
11. Keep original recordings and transcripts intact.
12. Validate all AI-generated structured data.
13. Never invent research references.
14. Never display fake progress or success messages.
15. Do not create nonfunctional buttons or placeholder features that appear complete.
16. Do not claim that cloud synchronization exists until it is connected and verified.
17. Do not claim that a feature works until it has been tested.
18. Keep Android functionality independent of the future web application.
19. Keep future backend integration possible through clean interfaces.
20. Make changes incrementally and verify the project after each major phase.

If you encounter a feature that requires an external API, backend, credential, or service that is not configured, implement the appropriate interface and local behavior where possible, and clearly document the remaining requirement.

Do not silently replace an unavailable capability with a fake implementation.

